    <string name="revamp_tip_0_title">Feed plants carefully</string>
    <string name="revamp_tip_0_body">Use a fertilizer made for your plant and follow its label. Compost kitchen scraps fully before using them; burying fresh food in an indoor pot can attract pests and damage roots.</string>
    <string name="revamp_tip_1_title">Repot when the plant needs it</string>
    <string name="revamp_tip_1_body">Roots circling the pot, water running straight through, or stalled growth can signal that it is time to repot. Move up only one pot size and water according to the plant’s needs.</string>
    <string name="revamp_tip_2_title">Keep leaves clean</string>
    <string name="revamp_tip_2_body">Wipe dusty leaves gently with water. Misting raises humidity only briefly, so humidity-loving plants may benefit more from grouping, a suitable humidifier, or a better location.</string>
    <string name="revamp_tip_3_title">Make plant care a calm routine</string>
    <string name="revamp_tip_3_body">A regular care routine can be enjoyable and grounding. Plants are not a treatment for stress or depression, but caring for them can be one small part of a supportive daily routine.</string>
    <string name="revamp_tip_4_title">Fresh air matters most</string>
    <string name="revamp_tip_4_body">A few houseplants do not replace ventilation or an air purifier. Open windows when conditions allow and address pollution sources directly; enjoy plants for the life and color they bring.</string>
    <string name="revamp_tip_5_title">Check below the surface</string>
    <string name="revamp_tip_5_body">The top of the soil can dry before the root zone. Check a few centimeters down with a finger or wooden stick, then match watering to the species instead of following a rigid calendar alone.</string>
    <string name="revamp_tip_6_title">Provide gentle air circulation</string>
    <string name="revamp_tip_6_body">Gentle airflow helps wet foliage and soil dry normally. Avoid strong hot or cold drafts, and give crowded plants enough space for air to move around their leaves.</string>
    <string name="revamp_more_actions">Plant care tools</string>
